parameters.text:
=You are a senior SEO copywriter and subject-matter editor writing for {{ ($json.site_description || {}).business_name || $json.business || 'this business' }}. Write the complete page by following the content brief exactly, in {{ $json.language_name || 'English' }} ({{ $json.spelling }} spelling), in a {{ $json.content_brief.tone || $json.tone || 'professional, direct' }} tone.

{{ ($json.style_guide || {}).prompt_block || '' }}

PAGE
Target Keyword: {{ $json.keyword }} · Country: {{ $json.country }} · Page Type: {{ $json.page_type }} · Goal: {{ $json.goal || 'leads' }}
{{ $json.existing_page ? 'This content replaces the existing page at ' + $json.existing_page.url + '. Keep every true fact from it; improve everything else.' : '' }}
{{ $json.ai_target ? 'AI ANSWER TARGET: this page must be the one AI assistants cite for "' + $json.ai_target.question + '". Answer that question in the first 40-60 words after the H1 (the Quick answer), give each search the assistants run (' + (($json.ai_target.fanout || []).map(f => '"' + f + '"').join(', ') || 'see the brief') + ') its own question-style H2 answered in its first sentence, keep any comparison neutral (never put this business first), and use only the verified figures with their linked sources.' : '' }}
{{ ($json.page_contract || {}).text || '' }}
{{ ($json.verdict_exclusions || []).length ? 'LEAVE OUT (the verdict on this keyword: these do not match what its buyers want; no section, heading or question about them): ' + $json.verdict_exclusions.map(e => e.topic).join('; ') + '.' : '' }}
{{ ($json.pricing_facts === false || $json.timeline_facts === false) ? 'NO ' + ($json.pricing_facts === false && $json.timeline_facts === false ? 'PRICES OR DURATIONS' : $json.pricing_facts === false ? 'PRICES' : 'DURATIONS') + ': the business has given no ' + ($json.pricing_facts === false && $json.timeline_facts === false ? 'price or timeline' : $json.pricing_facts === false ? 'price' : 'timeline') + ' facts. Write no ' + ($json.pricing_facts === false ? 'price, fee, fee band or rate' : '') + ($json.pricing_facts === false && $json.timeline_facts === false ? ', and no ' : '') + ($json.timeline_facts === false ? 'duration or timeline' : '') + ', and no bracket asking for one. Answer such a question with what drives it and what to ask a vendor.' : '' }}

WHO YOU ARE WRITING FOR
{{ $json.content_brief.target_audience || $json.audience || 'Not provided' }}
Pain points: {{ ($json.content_brief.audience_pain_points || []).join(' · ') }}
Objections to answer: {{ ($json.content_brief.objections || []).join(' · ') }}

WHAT MAKES THIS PAGE WIN
Unique angle: {{ $json.content_brief.unique_angle }}
Information gain (cover each fully; nobody else has it): {{ ($json.content_brief.information_gain || []).join(' · ') }}
Voice rules: {{ ($json.content_brief.voice_rules || []).join(' · ') }}

FACTS YOU MAY STATE AS TRUE
Client facts: {{ ($json.content_brief.client_facts || []).join(' · ') || 'none' }}
{{ $json.business_facts ? 'Facts given by the client: ' + $json.business_facts : '' }}
Verified external facts — cite ONLY these numbers, each with its source as a Markdown link [source](url):
{{ ($json.content_brief.evidence_plan || []).map(e => '- ' + e.fact + ' — ' + e.source_url).join('\n') || 'none: write no external number' }}
{{ $json.existing_page_text ? 'CURRENT PAGE (keep its true facts, dates, figures and named people; the whole page is given' + ($json.existing_page_text.length > 16000 ? ' up to its first 16,000 characters' : '') + '):\n' + ($json.existing_page_facts_text ? $json.existing_page_facts_text + '\n' : '') + ($json.existing_page_tables ? $json.existing_page_tables + '\n' : '') + $json.existing_page_text.slice(0, 16000) : '' }}
{{ (/united arab emirates/i.test($json.country || '') && /e-?invoic|peppol|\basp\b/i.test(($json.keyword || '') + ' ' + ($json.page_type || ''))) ?'WORDING: in the UAE the Ministry of Finance accredits e-invoicing service providers (the Federal Tax Authority administers the tax). Write "accredited under the Ministry of Finance\'s e-invoicing framework", never "FTA-accredited".' : '' }}

AUTHOR AND PROOF (E-E-A-T)
{{ $json.eeat_context || '' }}
Case studies you may cite (facts only as written; link a case study only when a URL is given): {{ $json.proof_context || 'none' }}
EXPERIENCE NOTES: weave each into the most relevant section as 1-3 sentences, using only what the facts, the case studies and the author's credentials above state. A note that asks for something nobody gave is left out (it is already a question for the client): never a bracket, never an invented experience, process or stance:
{{ (($json.content_brief || {}).experience_notes || []).map(n => '- ' + n).join('\n') || 'none' }}
{{ $json.role_writer || '' }}
{{ $json.video_context || '' }}

TERMS TO USE NATURALLY (term: minimum count): {{ ($json.content_brief.terms_to_use || []).map(t => t.term + ': ' + (t.min_count || 1)).join(', ') }}
SNIPPET TARGETS — each question becomes a heading followed immediately by a 40-60 word direct answer:
{{ ($json.content_brief.snippet_targets || []).map(s => '- ' + s.question + ' → ' + s.answer).join('\n') || 'none' }}

CONTENT BRIEF (outline, sections, key points, formats, target words)
{{ JSON.stringify({ h1: $json.content_brief.h1, meta_title: $json.content_brief.meta_title, meta_description: $json.content_brief.meta_description, slug: $json.content_brief.slug, primary_keyword: $json.content_brief.primary_keyword, secondary_keywords: $json.content_brief.secondary_keywords, answer_block: $json.content_brief.answer_block, outline: $json.content_brief.outline, comparison_table: $json.content_brief.comparison_table, image_suggestions: $json.content_brief.image_suggestions, faqs: $json.content_brief.faqs, cta: $json.content_brief.cta, target_word_count: $json.content_brief.target_word_count, proof_elements: $json.content_brief.proof_elements }, null, 1) }}

ALLOWED INTERNAL LINKS (use ONLY these URLs, exactly as written; if the list is empty, write no internal links)
{{ JSON.stringify(($json.content_brief || {}).internal_link_suggestions || [], null, 1) }}

OUTPUT FORMAT (Markdown, in this exact order)
Title: <meta_title, max 60 characters>
Meta Description: <meta_description, 120-155 characters>
Slug: <slug>
Primary Keyword: <primary_keyword>
Secondary Keywords: <comma separated>

# <h1>

<Introduction of 60-90 words: the primary keyword in the first sentence, the specific outcome the reader gets, no throat-clearing>

**Quick answer:** <the answer_block, 40-70 words, one paragraph, no placeholders>

Then every H2 from the outline, in order ("## " for H2, "### " for H3), each covering all its key points in its stated format and close to its target_words. Where the brief suggests an image, add a line: [Image: <alt text>]. Include the comparison table as a Markdown table in the most relevant section; compare what the reader can check (what each option covers, what it suits, what it needs from them), never a price or a timeline the facts do not state. Place the internal links naturally as [anchor](url).
Every question in the brief's "faqs" list becomes its own question-style heading ("### <the question>") inside the section it belongs to, answered immediately in 40-60 words, then the detail. Do NOT write a "Frequently Asked Questions" block, a Q1:/A1: list or any FAQ markup: Google stopped showing FAQ rich results in May 2026, while AI assistants quote a question heading with a direct answer under it.
The CTA section is always LAST and uses the brief's cta.
Aim for {{ $json.content_brief.target_word_count }} words of main content; the length is judged as the band in THE PAGE CONTRACT above.

WRITING RULES — these decide the quality
1. Specific beats general. Every section contains at least two of: a concrete example, a number with its linked source, a numbered step list, a decision rule ("choose X if…"), a mistake to avoid with its consequence, or a client fact.
2. No filler. Never use: "in today's fast-paced world", "ever-evolving landscape", "delve", "dive into", "unlock", "unleash", "seamless", "seamlessly", "robust", "leverage", "cutting-edge", "game-changer", "game-changing", "revolutionize", "elevate", "empower", "navigate the complexities", "look no further", "it's important to note", "at the end of the day", "in conclusion", "comprehensive solution", "tailored solutions", "harness the power", "whether you're a", "a testament to", "crucial", "paramount", "realm", "tapestry", "embark", "foster", "streamline", "synergy", "holistic", "best-in-class", "world-class", "state-of-the-art", "top-notch", "one-stop shop", "in this article", "without further ado", "unparalleled", "transformative", "stay ahead of the curve", "when it comes to", "a wide range of".
3. Voice: talk to the reader as "you", active voice, plain words, sentences of 8-22 words with variety, paragraphs of 1-4 sentences, no rhetorical questions in body text, no exclamation marks, no bold inside paragraphs except the Quick answer label.
4. Facts: state a number only if it is in the verified facts or client facts, then link its source. Where a business-specific number (price, timeline, count, award, review, guarantee) is missing, rewrite the sentence so it does not need one: what drives the cost, which choices change the timeline, what to ask a vendor for. Never write a square-bracket placeholder or note of any kind ([Price], [Timeline], [Confirm: ...], [Author insight: ...]): a page with a bracket in it cannot be published. Never write the word "placeholder".
5. Headings are descriptive and scannable, use the snippet-target questions as headings where given, and never copy competitor headings.
5b. Every sentence is written from scratch. The draft is compared with every competitor page that was read and with this site's own pages: more than 15% of it matching one page in runs of eight words or more fails the quality check and comes back for a rewrite. Cover the same ground where the brief asks for it, in our own words, order and examples — never reuse a competitor's sentences, lists, table rows or definitions, and never repeat passages of another page of this website.
6. Use the primary keyword in the H1, the first sentence, at least two H2s and the final section; otherwise write naturally and never stuff.
7. Show expertise: explain the why behind each recommendation, name the trade-offs, and give the reader a way to decide. Give each information-gain item its own full treatment.
8. No schema, script or HTML. No production notes, layout notes, image briefs or commentary anywhere: after the Secondary Keywords line the next line is the H1. Return only the Markdown, starting with the Title line.
9. Length: stay inside the band in THE PAGE CONTRACT. Finish every section and the CTA; if space is tight, shorten sections rather than dropping the ending.
10. Sources: every external number is quoted exactly as its source writes it and carries that source's link. Prefer an official, government, standards or major research / press source; a vendor or agency blog may be used at most once on the whole page. Never add tracking parameters (utm_*, srsltid, gclid, fbclid) to a link. A number you cannot find in the verified facts above does not go on the page.

parameters.jsCode:
// ---- the page type, as one of the options the form offers (D10, 2026-10-12; the builders inline this file where a node asks for the PAGE_TYPE kit) ----
// The verdict and the keyword screen answer in free text: the live page of execution 365 was planned as "Service Page (ERP implementation
// UAE) with built-in vendor-neutral comparison, cost and compliance sections". That sentence then travelled as the page type into the brief
// (which read it as a guide and set 3,100 words), into the schema and into meta.json. PT.of() maps any such text to one of the fixed options
// and PT.notes() keeps the sentence itself, so nothing the verdict said is lost — it reaches the brief as page_notes instead.
const PT = (() => {
  const TYPES = ['Service Page', 'Product Page', 'Blog Post', 'Landing Page', 'Guide', 'Pillar Page', 'Local Page', 'Case Study'];
  // first match wins by POSITION in the text, not by rule order: "Service Page (…) with built-in vendor-neutral comparison" is a service
  // page that also compares, not a comparison guide.
  const RULES = [[/case stud/i, 'Case Study'], [/\bpillar\b|\bhub\b|topic cluster/i, 'Pillar Page'], [/\blocal\b|city page|area page/i, 'Local Page'],
    [/\bproducts?\b|e-?commerce|\bshop\b|\bstore\b|catalou?g/i, 'Product Page'], [/landing|lead capture|campaign page|squeeze/i, 'Landing Page'],
    [/\bblogs?\b|\bnews\b|\barticles?\b|\bposts?\b/i, 'Blog Post'],
    [/\bguides?\b|how.?to|tutorial|comparison|compare|versus|\bvs\b|\bfaqs?\b|resource|checklist|listicle|round.?up|explainer|glossary/i, 'Guide'],
    [/\bservices?\b|solution|category|collection|offering/i, 'Service Page']];
  const of = (v, dflt) => {
    const t = String(v == null ? '' : v).trim();
    const fallback = TYPES.find(x => x.toLowerCase() === String(dflt || '').trim().toLowerCase()) || 'Service Page';
    if (!t) return fallback;
    const exact = TYPES.find(x => x.toLowerCase() === t.toLowerCase());
    if (exact) return exact;
    let best = null;
    for (const r of RULES) { const i = t.search(r[0]); if (i >= 0 && (!best || i < best.i)) best = { i: i, type: r[1] }; }
    return best ? best.type : fallback;
  };
  // the free text, kept for the brief; empty when it says nothing beyond the type itself (the form's own wording included)
  const SAME = ['pillar / hub page', 'pillar/hub page', 'hub page', 'local page (city or area)', 'case study page'];
  const notes = (v, type) => {
    const t = String(v == null ? '' : v).trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
    if (!t) return '';
    const bare = t.replace(/[.\s]+$/, '').toLowerCase();
    if (bare === String(type || '').toLowerCase() || TYPES.some(x => x.toLowerCase() === bare) || SAME.indexOf(bare) >= 0) return '';
    return t.slice(0, 300);
  };
  return { of: of, notes: notes, TYPES: TYPES };
})();
// 2026-10-13 (re-rating §3.2 "Also seen"): a ladder row written before D10 carries free text as its page type
// ("Service Page (ERP implementation UAE) with built-in vendor-neutral comparison…"), and the cadence / "Write now" body passed it
// straight on. PT.of maps anything to one of the form's options, PT.notes keeps the sentence for the brief.
// v4: validation errors no longer crash the run. They are returned as { validation_error } and shown to the
// user (form completion page) or returned as HTTP 400 (API). See "Input OK?" right after Rate Limit.
let __via_webhook = false;
try { $('Start Form').first(); } catch (e) { __via_webhook = true; }
const __main = () => {
// ===================== CONFIG (edit here only) =====================
const CONFIG = {
  brand: "Alaventra",   // from n8n/.env (SEO_BRAND) at build time; shown on reports and e-mails
  crawl_max_pages: 200,             // DataForSEO on-page crawl size (also used when reading crawled pages)
  crawl_js: false,                  // true = render JavaScript during the crawl (slower, costs more)
  qa_max_rounds: 5,   // H1 (2026-10-27): the Copywriter's draft + up to 3 section-targeted edits + the final check (Page Candidates keeps the best draft; a full-page second pass inflated length, a section edit cannot)                 // how many times the Editor may revise content that fails QA
  default_country: 'United States',
  ai_budget_usd: 15,                // estimated Claude spend allowed per budget period (see Rate Limit); 3 → 10 on 2026-10-01 for the system test, 6 from 2026-10-02, 15 since 2026-10-15 at the owner's request (cost is not the constraint, the result is) — the Anthropic Console workspace limit is the hard cap
  ai_budget_period: 'day',          // 'day' | 'month' — daily window while testing; the Anthropic Console workspace limit is the hard cap
  // (2026-10-15, benchmark area 13): the same guard for the DataForSEO money, over the same period. It was unguarded until now, and it is
  // where most of the spend is ($2.3876 of the $3.63 the 2026-10-14 re-rating cost). `dfs_balance_floor_usd` is what the account must keep
  // after a run: below it the run is refused rather than started, because a run that exhausts the account mid-flight delivers half a report
  // and charges for all of it. A balance reading that did not answer is 0 and refuses nothing — a guard that cannot measure must not block.
  dfs_budget_usd: 15,
  dfs_balance_floor_usd: 0.5,
  // P34-5 (2026-10-12): how long a run may hold its budget reservation before it is released as `stale` (two audits killed by the
  // task runner held $0.77 of the day's estimate for ever), and the crawl size from which only one audit of a site may run at a time.
  // G5 (2026-10-13): how much of a draft may be word for word the same as ONE page it was written from (the 10-15% convention of
  // the similarity checkers). Over this, *Originality Check* fails the quality check and the editor rewrites those passages.
  originality_max_overlap_pct: 15,
  run_stale_hours: 2,
  heavy_audit_pages: 100,
  // G8 / K4 (2026-10-13): how many keywords discovery checks live on Google for intent, page type and who ranks. One check is a
  // DataForSEO live-advanced SERP at depth 10 (about $0.002), so 16 costs ~$0.032 a run; KWI.liveChecks caps it at 25.
  live_serp_checks: 16,
  // G14 (2026-10-13): how many key pages of an audit are read twice — the raw first response and the rendered page — so the
  // report can say what only exists after JavaScript. Both fetches are free (a plain GET and one render); 5 covers the homepage
  // plus the four pages Search Console says earn the most.
  render_diff_pages: 5,
  // B5-5 (2026-10-15): how many of the known URLs the crawl never reached are read with a free plain GET, so "not crawled"
  // becomes a statement instead of a count. 0 switches the check off for a site; 50 is the ceiling.
  not_crawled_checks: 25,
  ladder_pages_default: 1,          // ladder mode: pages written immediately (1-3; each page is its own content run)
  ladder_tracker_cadence: 'weekly', // the Rank Tracker workflow runs weekly; 'monthly' is documentation only until its schedule is changed
  ladder_auto_next_rung: false,     // false = the tracker recommends the next rung (one-click form link + API body); true is not wired
  wordpress_publish: false          // true + wordpress_url in the request = every generated page is also created as a WordPress DRAFT
};

// DataForSEO location codes are 2000 + ISO-3166 numeric code
const COUNTRIES = {
  'United States':        { code: 2840, iso: 'US', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'American English',   currency: 'USD' },
  'United Kingdom':       { code: 2826, iso: 'GB', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'GBP' },
  'Canada':               { code: 2124, iso: 'CA', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'Canadian English',   currency: 'CAD' },
  'Australia':            { code: 2036, iso: 'AU', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'Australian English', currency: 'AUD' },
  'New Zealand':          { code: 2554, iso: 'NZ', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'NZD' },
  'Ireland':              { code: 2372, iso: 'IE', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'EUR' },
  'Pakistan':             { code: 2586, iso: 'PK', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'PKR' },
  'India':                { code: 2356, iso: 'IN', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'INR' },
  'United Arab Emirates': { code: 2784, iso: 'AE', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'AED' },
  'Saudi Arabia':         { code: 2682, iso: 'SA', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'SAR' },
  'Singapore':            { code: 2702, iso: 'SG', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'SGD' },
  'South Africa':         { code: 2710, iso: 'ZA', lang: 'en', language: 'English', spelling: 'British English',    currency: 'ZAR' },
  'Germany':              { code: 2276, iso: 'DE', lang: 'de', language: 'German',  spelling: 'German',             currency: 'EUR' },
  'France':               { code: 2250, iso: 'FR', lang: 'fr', language: 'French',  spelling: 'French',             currency: 'EUR' },
  'Spain':                { code: 2724, iso: 'ES', lang: 'es', language: 'Spanish', spelling: 'European Spanish',   currency: 'EUR' },
  'Italy':                { code: 2380, iso: 'IT', lang: 'it', language: 'Italian', spelling: 'Italian',            currency: 'EUR' },
  'Netherlands':          { code: 2528, iso: 'NL', lang: 'nl', language: 'Dutch',   spelling: 'Dutch',              currency: 'EUR' },
  'Brazil':               { code: 2076, iso: 'BR', lang: 'pt', language: 'Portuguese', spelling: 'Brazilian Portuguese', currency: 'BRL' },
  'Mexico':               { code: 2484, iso: 'MX', lang: 'es', language: 'Spanish', spelling: 'Mexican Spanish',    currency: 'MXN' }
};
// ===================================================================

let p1, raw, via_webhook;
try {
  p1 = $('Start Form').first().json;
  raw = $input.first().json;
  via_webhook = false;
} catch (e) {
  // No Start Form in this execution -> triggered by the Webhook
  p1 = { 'What do you want?': 'I know my keyword' };
  raw = $input.first().json || {};
  via_webhook = true;
}
// n8n's Webhook node wraps the payload as { headers, params, query, body }
const p2 = (raw && raw.body && typeof raw.body === 'object' && !Array.isArray(raw.body)) ? raw.body : (raw || {});

function pick(obj, ...words) {
  const key = Object.keys(obj || {}).find(k =>
    words.every(w => k.toLowerCase().replace(/[\s_-]+/g, ' ').includes(w))
  );
  return key ? obj[key] : '';
}
function asArray(v) {
  if (Array.isArray(v)) return v;
  if (typeof v === 'string' && v) return v.split(/[,\n]/).map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  return [];
}
function cleanDomain(v) {
  return String(v || '').trim().toLowerCase()
    .replace(/^https?:\/\//, '').replace(/^www\./, '').replace(/[\/?#].*$/, '').replace(/:\d+$/, '');
}
// Public hostnames only: no IP literals, no localhost/internal names (SSRF guard)
const domainOk = (d) => {
  if (!d || d.length > 253) return false;
  if (/^(\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}$/.test(d)) return false;
  if (/^\[?[0-9a-f:]+\]?$/.test(d) && d.includes(':')) return false;
  if (/(^|\.)(localhost|local|internal|localdomain|home|lan|corp|intranet|test|example|invalid)$/.test(d)) return false;
  return /^([a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?\.)+(xn--[a-z0-9-]+|[a-z]{2,24})$/.test(d);
};

// ---------- Mode ----------
const choice = String(pick(p1, 'what', 'want') || '').toLowerCase();
let mode = 'discover';
let verdict_only = false;
if (choice.includes('check') && choice.includes('keyword')) { mode = 'keyword'; verdict_only = true; }
else if (choice.includes('know')) mode = 'keyword';
else if (choice.includes('describe')) mode = 'site_description';
else if (choice.includes('audit')) mode = 'audit';
else if (choice.includes('rank my site') || choice.includes('ladder')) mode = 'ladder';
else if (choice.includes('track')) mode = 'track';
else if (choice.includes('published')) mode = 'published';
else if (choice.includes('check-in') || choice.includes('checkin')) mode = 'checkin';
else if (choice.includes('case study')) mode = 'case_study';
else if (choice.includes('business profile')) mode = 'profile';
else if (choice.includes('ai visibility')) mode = 'ai_visibility';
else if (choice.includes('backlink')) mode = 'backlinks';
if (via_webhook) {
  const m = String(p2.mode || '').toLowerCase();
  if (m === 'verdict' || m === 'check') { mode = 'keyword'; verdict_only = true; }
  else if (m === 'audit') mode = 'audit';
  else if (m === 'discover') mode = 'discover';
  else if (m === 'describe') mode = 'site_description';
  else if (m === 'ladder') mode = 'ladder';
  else if (m === 'track') mode = 'track';
  else if (m === 'published') mode = 'published';
  else if (m === 'checkin' || m === 'check-in') mode = 'checkin';
  else if (m === 'case_study' || m === 'case-study' || m === 'casestudy') mode = 'case_study';
  else if (m === 'profile') mode = 'profile';
  else if (m === 'ai_visibility' || m === 'ai-visibility' || m === 'ai') mode = 'ai_visibility';
  else if (m === 'backlinks' || m === 'links') mode = 'backlinks';
}

// ---------- Country (name or ISO-2 code) ----------
const countryRaw = String(pick(p2, 'country') || '').trim();
let countryName = Object.keys(COUNTRIES).find(n => n.toLowerCase() === countryRaw.toLowerCase())
  || Object.keys(COUNTRIES).find(n => COUNTRIES[n].iso === countryRaw.toUpperCase())
  || (mode === 'site_description' ? CONFIG.default_country : '');
const c = COUNTRIES[countryName] || null;
if (!['site_description', 'published', 'checkin', 'profile'].includes(mode) && !c) throw new Error('Please select a Target Country.');   // published-page reports and check-ins need no market

// ---------- Domain / email ----------
const domain = cleanDomain(pick(p2, 'domain') || pick(p2, 'website'));
if (domain && !domainOk(domain)) throw new Error('Please enter a public website address like example.com');

const email = String(pick(p2, 'email') || '').trim().toLowerCase();
if (email && !/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(email)) throw new Error('Please enter a valid email address.');

const callback_url = String(pick(p2, 'callback') || '').trim();
if (callback_url && !/^(https:\/\/[^\s]+|http:\/\/(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|host\.docker\.internal|n8n)(:\d+)?\/[^\s]*)$/.test(callback_url)) throw new Error('callback_url must be an https URL (plain http is allowed only for localhost while testing).');

const competitors = asArray(pick(p2, 'competitor')).map(cleanDomain).filter(domainOk).filter(d => d !== domain).slice(0, 3);

// ---------- Other fields ----------
const features = asArray(pick(p2, 'feature')).map(f => String(f).toLowerCase());
const wants = asArray(pick(p2, 'receive')).map(w => String(w).toLowerCase());
const reportType = String(pick(p2, 'report type') || pick(p2, 'report_type') || '').toLowerCase();
